WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:02.230
A bomb goes off.

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:08.660
Then the familiar scenes of rescue, rubble,
and the dead, dying and wounded.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.080
Another fatal day in Afghanistan.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:18.170
Like on Monday: a suicide bombing in the capital
Kabul killed six people - nearly 100 more

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.480
were killed elsewhere around the country.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.780
The United Nations estimates more than 8,000
people have been killed and wounded during

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:30.340
the first nine months of 2018 alone.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:35.760
Still, the German government has not budged
on its deportation policy.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.719
Afghan refugees can be sent back - against
their will, if necessary.

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:42.690
This, human rights groups strongly disagree
with - and are trying to stop.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:49.960
In our view, Germany is violating international
law and the European Convention on Human Rights

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:54.510
by deporting people to Afghanistan.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.730
That's because those laws prohibit deportation
to unsafe countries.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:02.969
The German government, however, says parts
of Afghanistan are safe - even if the country

00:01:02.969 --> 00:01:04.739
as a whole is not.

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:09.680
The government is more cautious when it comes
its own citizens visiting Afghanistan: Violence

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.380
affects "all parts" of the country, according
to the Foreign Office's long-standing travel

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:15.659
warning.

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:19.960
German authorities are tight-lipped when deportations
are carried out - often at night and out of

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:20.960
public view.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.360
They declined to confirm the most recently
reported deportation flight, with federal

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:29.280
police telling DW only that a "repatriation
action" was in the works.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:34.640
The Interior Ministry does not comment so
as "not to endanger the implementation and

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.280
success of a repatriation action."

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:44.270
Groups like Amnesty International want forced
repatriations to end.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.469
We recently submitted to Interior Minister
Horst Seehofer a petition with nearly 30,000

00:01:47.469 --> 00:01:57.340
signatures in Germany, demanding an end to
all deportations to Afghanistan.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.229
The Interior Ministry has yet to respond to
the petition.

